{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788336561267108001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"beige-acute-bobolink","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"89e049be178fec40b84c73671fdbdc3ea2e801af3f48891ac7bce6e3f083b223","event_uuid":"ee94fe49-ac64-4370-bccf-e0d81b215c35","position":{"commit_sha":"c0a7ed26c0ec9842cec75f9612cc2fdbbcc38e51","position":"1788332684139080595-ee94fe49-ac64-4370-bccf-e0d81b215c35"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f5983a5bb861de9bb9af95aae808d0d0881145bd1b5e920c90303c43004fa89a","event_uuid":"b0ea23e5-75ff-4af8-8351-5845cb6fb0f9","position":{"commit_sha":"e24f2e251d3e4694d6380360174322b96e0aeed6","position":"1788332748552439175-b0ea23e5-75ff-4af8-8351-5845cb6fb0f9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8ad34b6b33825b5feaffe4bf807bab1fd2914711c0173c5ea3edf0b58e19a330","event_uuid":"7af0a8d0-e56e-4a6d-94db-5568f4bba6a2","position":{"commit_sha":"6526264f8ebd3a19b4ef34dea251507b13322ee4","position":"1788332821191844287-7af0a8d0-e56e-4a6d-94db-5568f4bba6a2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788332684139080595,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7af0a8d0-e56e-4a6d-94db-5568f4bba6a2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"65dd-e93b-666a-4caa"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`gate_status(job_id)` reports a run as terminal (`status: \"passed\"`, with a `verdict`) before\nthat run's `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar is readable from the tickets tracker. The documented\npoll-then-read workflow — start a gate with `review_plan_start`, poll `gate_status`, then read\nthe findings to remediate — therefore has a window in which the caller reads the PREVIOUS\nrun's findings and believes they are the ones just reported.\n\nThis is silent: nothing distinguishes a freshly-written sidecar from a stale one at read time,\nso the caller acts on findings it has already addressed.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nObserved 2026-09-01 while remediating `responsive-undamaged-auklet` (`549b-9cc5-940e-46c3`).\n\n1. `review_plan_start responsive-undamaged-auklet` returned\n   `job_id 1788326596882647223-94573cf0d90d404e87c74855306c16f2`, whose id prefix places the\n   start at 22:23:16.\n2. After the run, `gate_status` on that job returned `status: \"passed\"`, `verdict: \"BLOCK\"` —\n   polled twice, both terminal.\n3. At that moment the newest sidecar under `.tickets-tracker/549b-9cc5-940e-46c3/` was\n   `1788325963941841589-…-REVIEW_RESULT.json` (22:12:43), which belongs to the PRIOR run, and\n   the directory held 6 sidecars for 6 completed runs minus one.\n4. Reading \"the latest findings\" therefore returned the prior run's two findings verbatim.\n5. Re-checked later: `1788327281362056852-…-REVIEW_RESULT.json` (22:34:41) was present, with\n   the actual findings for that job, and the count reconciled.\n\nExpected: once `gate_status` reports a terminal verdict for a job, that job's sidecar is\nreadable — or the response says the record is not yet durable. Actual: terminal status is\nreported while the sidecar for that job is still absent.\n\nThe consequence is not hypothetical: in this session it produced a remediation pass aimed at\nfindings that had already been fixed, and only a timestamp comparison between the job id and\nthe sidecar filename revealed the mismatch.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe gate-run status surface and its relationship to sidecar durability:\n`src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py` (the run index that `gate_status` replays) and the plan-review\nsidecar write path. Either the terminal transition waits on the sidecar write, or\n`gate_status` exposes whether this job's sidecar is readable yet.\n\nNote `gate_status` already carries a `durable` block for the signed ATTESTATION. That block\nreports attestation currency, not sidecar readability, and on a BLOCK verdict it is\n`unsigned` by definition — so it cannot be used to distinguish \"findings ready\" from\n\"findings not yet written\".\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Changing when a verdict is computed, or the verdict itself.\n- Making sidecar recording non-best-effort in a way that would fail a run whose findings\n  failed to persist; the verdict must still be reported.\n- The `plan_review_status` / attestation currency semantics.\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nAdditive if solved by exposing readability on the status response; behavior-narrowing if\nsolved by deferring the terminal transition until the sidecar lands. Either way no stored\nevent shape changes and back-out is reverting the status surface. Existing callers that\nignore the new field keep working.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests against the real run-index replay with a stubbed sidecar writer, driving the\nwindow explicitly: assert the status contract holds while the sidecar is absent and after it\nlands. The race is made deterministic by controlling the writer rather than by timing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] With a job whose verdict is recorded but whose sidecar has not been written,\n      `gate_status` does not present that job as having readable findings — either it is not\n      yet terminal, or the response carries an explicit not-yet-readable indicator; verified\n      by `pytest` with a stubbed writer held open, asserting the returned fields.\n- [ ] Once the sidecar for that job is written, `gate_status` reports terminal AND readable,\n      and the sidecar whose event id corresponds to that job is the newest for the ticket;\n      verified by `pytest` asserting both after releasing the stubbed writer.\n- [ ] A caller following the documented poll-then-read sequence never observes a prior run's\n      findings as the current job's; verified by `pytest` driving two successive runs over a\n      seeded store and asserting the findings read after each poll belong to that run's id.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n`make lint`, `make typecheck` and `make test` pass; the documented poll-then-read sequence\ncannot return a prior run's findings for a job reported terminal.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py","reason":"The durable run index gate_status replays; the terminal transition or the reported shape must account for sidecar readability."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"The gate_status MCP read surface that reports status and verdict to the polling caller."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_status_sidecar_visibility.py","reason":"Unit tests holding a stubbed sidecar writer open to make the window deterministic, asserting the status contract before and after the write lands."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["mcp","plan-review","gate-runs"],"ticket_id":"01c4-cca2-ec11-4530","ticket_type":"bug","title":"gate_status reports a terminal verdict before its REVIEW_RESULT sidecar is readable","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ee94fe49-ac64-4370-bccf-e0d81b215c35","b0ea23e5-75ff-4af8-8351-5845cb6fb0f9","7af0a8d0-e56e-4a6d-94db-5568f4bba6a2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788336561267108001,"uuid":"862d5dbe-52e0-4773-a759-060142e206fc"}